.TH RUFUS-CLI 1 2026-10-27 "Rufus 4.16" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rufus\-cli \- create bootable USB drives from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rufus\-cli
.RB [ \-v ]
.B list
.RB [ \-\-hdd ]
.RB [ \-\-non\-usb ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B rufus\-cli
.RB [ \-v ]
.B write
.I DEVICE
.RB [ \-\-image
.IR FILE ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B rufus\-cli
.RB [ \-v ]
.B cycle
.I DEVICE
.br
.B rufus\-cli
.RB [ \-v ]
.B save
.I DEVICE FILE
.br
.B rufus\-cli
.RB [ \-v ]
.B save\-optical
.I FILE
.br
.B rufus\-cli
.RB [ \-v ]
.B download
.RI [ VERSION
.RI [ RELEASE
.RI [ EDITION
.RI [ LANGUAGE
.RI [ ARCH ]]]]]
.RB [ \-o
.IR FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rufus\-cli
does what the window of
.BR rufus (1)
does, with the same rules for the options that are left out. Its questions are
asked on the terminal, or answered with
.BR \-\-yes .
The commands that write to a drive go through
.BR rufus\-helper ,
which
.BR pkexec (1)
starts as root (unless
.B rufus\-cli
already runs as root).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List the drives that Rufus can write to, with the loop devices of files.
.B \-\-hdd
also lists USB hard drives,
.B \-\-non\-usb
non-USB removable drives, and
.B \-\-json
gives the list as JSON.
.TP
.BI write " DEVICE"
Write to a drive (such as
.BR /dev/sdb ),
with the defaults of the main window for what the options leave out.
.TP
.BI cycle " DEVICE"
Disconnect a USB drive and connect it again (Alt\-C in the window).
.TP
.BI save " DEVICE FILE"
Save a drive to an image: a fixed VHD (\fI.vhd\fR), a dynamic VHDX
(\fI.vhdx\fR), or an ISO of the files of its first volume (\fI.iso\fR, with
.BR xorriso (1)).
.TP
.BI save\-optical " FILE"
Save the disc of an optical drive to an ISO image.
.TP
.B download
Download a Windows or UEFI Shell ISO, as Fido does. The choices of the next
step get listed, until the URL of the ISO, which
.B \-o
.I FILE
downloads. The choices are numbers (from 1) or the start of their names.
.SH WRITE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-image " FILE"
The image to write: an ISO, a disk image (raw, or compressed with gzip, xz,
bzip2, zstd, lzma or zip), a VHD or a VHDX.
.TP
.BI \-\-boot " TYPE"
non\-bootable, image (the default with
.BR \-\-image ),
freedos, msdos, syslinux4, syslinux6, reactos, grub2, grub4dos or uefi\-ntfs.
.TP
.BI \-\-partition " STYLE"
mbr, gpt or sfd (a super floppy, without partition table).
.TP
.BI \-\-target " SYSTEM"
bios or uefi.
.TP
.BI \-\-fs " NAME"
FAT, FAT32, NTFS, UDF, exFAT, ext2, ext3 or ext4.
.TP
.BI \-\-cluster " BYTES"
The cluster size.
.TP
.BI \-\-label " TEXT"
The volume label.
.TP
.BI \-\-persistence " MB"
The size of a persistent partition, for the Linux images that support one.
.TP
.BI \-\-archive " FILE"
A zip archive to extract to the drive (FAT, NTFS, exFAT or UDF).
.TP
.B \-\-slow
A full format (which zeroes the volume) rather than a quick one.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-extended\-label
No autorun.inf label and icon.
.TP
.B \-\-old\-bios\-fixes
Add fixes for old BIOSes.
.TP
.B \-\-dual
Windows images boot with BIOS and UEFI (Alt\-E in the window).
.TP
.BI \-\-bad\-blocks " PASSES"
Check for bad blocks first: 1, 2, slc, mlc or tlc.
.TP
.BR \-\-iso ", " \-\-dd
How to write an ISOHybrid image (asked otherwise).
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Answer the other questions, and the confirmation, with their first choice.
.TP
.BR \-\-hdd ", " \-\-non\-usb
As for
.BR list .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Display the log on the standard error (twice for the USB debug messages).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display the commands and options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUFUS_HELPER
The path of the helper, instead of the one of the installation.
.TP
.B RUFUS_LOCALE
The language of the ISOs that
.B download
proposes first, such as
.B pl\-PL
(the one of the locale otherwise).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 for a wrong command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Write an ISO to a USB drive, as the window would, without questions:
.PP
.RS
.B rufus\-cli write /dev/sdb \-\-image ubuntu.iso \-\-yes
.RE
.PP
Write a Windows 11 ISO for a BIOS computer:
.PP
.RS
.B rufus\-cli write /dev/sdb \-\-image Win11.iso \-\-partition mbr \-\-target bios
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rufus (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
https://github.com/mikigal/rufus\-linux
